img = cv2.imread("street.png")
equalized = cv2.equalizeHist(img)', 'python', '', '`cv2.equalizeHist()` works on **one channel**. A colour image read with `imread` has three (B, G, R), so OpenCV refuses it. Either convert with `cvtColor` or read the image directly in grayscale with `cv2.imread("street.png", cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)`.', 'easy', 'auto', '{"shuffle":true}', 1, 'published', 0, 1792108800000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
