print(marks)', 'python', '', '`marks.append(18)` adds 18 to the end of the List, so for a moment the List is `[12, 15, 18]`. But `append()` **returns nothing**: its result is the special value `None`. Line 2 then stores that `None` in `marks`, and the List is lost.

Call `append()` on a line of its own, without `=`:

```python
marks.append(18)
```', 'medium', 'auto', '{"shuffle":true}', 1, 'published', 0, 1791504000000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
