```
Course: Programming Applications
Lecture: 1
Language: Python
```

Use a comma in the second `print` to print the number 1 after the text `Lecture:`.', '# write your comment here
', 'python', 'The program reads nothing and prints the three lines above, exactly as shown.', 'Each `print` starts a new line, so three lines need three `print` calls. Text goes in quotes. In the second line, the comma puts a space between `Lecture:` and the number `1`. The comment on the first line starts with `#`, so Python skips it; it only tells people what the program is for.', 'easy', 'reference_review', '{"compare":"trim_trailing"}', 1, 'published', 0, 1792022400000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
