INSERT INTO exercises (id, course_id, topic_id, lesson_id, slug, type, title, prompt_md, code, code_language, expected_behavior_md, explanation_md, difficulty, grading_mode, settings, points, status, is_demo, updated_at) VALUES ('exe_cb5531af671b4b37', 'course_programming_fundamentals', 'top_a369e9ead4fd7321', 'les_a369e9ead4fd7321', 'final-m2-types-trace-saved-bool', 'trace', 'A bool saved too early', 'A `bool` box can store the answer of a comparison: `true` or `false`. This program saves such an answer, then changes the temperature, then copies it into an `int`. Watch **when** each box gets its value and what each type can hold. What exactly does it print? Type one line of output per line.', '#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    float temperature = 29.5;
    bool hot = temperature > 30;
    temperature = temperature + 1;
    cout << temperature << " " << hot << endl;
    hot = temperature > 30;
    cout << hot << endl;
    int whole = temperature;
    cout << whole << " " << (whole > 30) << endl;
    cout << (whole == temperature) << endl;
    return 0;
}', 'cpp', '', '- **Line 6** works out `29.5 > 30` **once**, when that line runs. The answer, FALSE, is stored in `hot`. A `bool` box holds a value, not the question, so when line 7 makes the temperature 30.5, `hot` is still `false`. `cout` prints `false` as `0`, so line 8 prints `30.5 0`.
- **Line 9** asks the question again with the new temperature: `30.5 > 30` is TRUE, so `hot` becomes `true` and prints as `1`.
- **Line 11** stores 30.5 in an `int`. An `int` holds whole numbers only, so the `.5` is dropped (not rounded): `whole` is 30. Then `30 > 30` is FALSE, printed as `0`. The `int` copy gives a different answer from the `float`, even though both came from the same temperature.
- **Line 13** compares 30 with 30.5. They are not equal, so it prints `0`.', 'hard', 'auto', '{"reserved":true,"compare":"trim_trailing","caseSensitive":true}', 1, 'published', 0, 1791590400000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
