INSERT INTO exercises (id, course_id, topic_id, lesson_id, slug, type, title, prompt_md, code, code_language, expected_behavior_md, explanation_md, difficulty, grading_mode, settings, points, status, is_demo, updated_at) VALUES ('exe_5ca46ad67b947314', 'course_programming_fundamentals', 'top_af5d78b3c9083abc', 'les_9962b1823b489bb3', 'final-m3-dowhile-trace-count-digits', 'trace', 'How many digits does 0 have?', 'A phone shop counts the digits of a code by removing the last digit with `n / 10` until nothing is left. The program counts the digits of 0 twice, once with a `do-while` and once with a `while`, and then counts the digits of 3050. Trace it by hand. What exactly does it print? Type one line of output per line.', '#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int n = 0;
    int a = 0;
    do
    {
        a++;
        n = n / 10;
    }
    while (n > 0);
    n = 0;
    int b = 0;
    while (n > 0)
    {
        b++;
        n = n / 10;
    }
    cout << a << " " << b << endl;
    n = 3050;
    a = 0;
    do
    {
        a++;
        n = n / 10;
        cout << n << " ";
    }
    while (n > 0);
    cout << endl << a << endl;
    return 0;
}', 'cpp', '', '**The first two loops, with n = 0.**

- The `do-while` runs its body first: `a` becomes 1 and `n` stays 0 (0 / 10 is 0). Only then is `0 > 0` checked; it is FALSE, so the loop stops after **one** pass. `a` is 1.
- The `while` loop checks `0 > 0` first. It is FALSE, so the body runs **zero** times and `b` stays 0.

So the first line is `1 0`. The number 0 is written with one digit, so here the `do-while` gives the right count and the `while` loop doesn''t: counting digits is a job where the body must run at least once.

**The third loop, with n = 3050.** Each pass counts one digit, removes the last digit, and prints what is left:

| Pass | a | n after `n / 10` | `n > 0`? |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 | 305 | TRUE |
| 2 | 2 | 30 | TRUE |
| 3 | 3 | 3 | TRUE |
| 4 | 4 | 0 | FALSE |

The second line is `305 30 3 0 ` (each number is followed by a space), and after the loop `endl` ends that line, so `4` is printed on its own line. The zeros inside 3050 are digits too, so they are counted.', 'hard', 'auto', '{"reserved":true,"compare":"trim_trailing","caseSensitive":true}', 1, 'published', 0, 1791590400000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
