INSERT INTO exercises (id, course_id, topic_id, lesson_id, slug, type, title, prompt_md, code, code_language, expected_behavior_md, explanation_md, difficulty, grading_mode, settings, points, status, is_demo, updated_at) VALUES ('exe_4f50cdce69665c3a', 'course_programming_fundamentals', 'top_a4b48227d1aff1d2', 'les_a4b48227d1aff1d2', 'final-m3-for-trace-double-plus-one', 'trace', 'An update that doubles and adds one', 'The update of a `for` loop doesn''t have to be `i++` or `i += 2`. Here it is `i = i * 2 + 1`. The variable `i` is declared **before** the loop, so it can still be printed after the loop ends. Trace the program by hand. What exactly does it print? Type one line of output per line.', '#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int count = 0;
    int i;
    for (i = 2; i < 50; i = i * 2 + 1)
    {
        cout << i << " ";
        count++;
    }
    cout << endl;
    cout << count << " passes, i = " << i << endl;
    return 0;
}', 'cpp', '', 'The initialization `i = 2` runs once. After each pass the update `i = i * 2 + 1` runs (multiply first, then add 1), and then the condition is checked:

2 → 5 → 11 → 23 → 47 → 95

The values 2, 5, 11, 23 and 47 are all less than 50, so the body runs **5** times and prints each of them followed by a space, all on one line. After 47 the update makes `i` 95, and `95 < 50` is FALSE, so 95 is never printed inside the loop.

Because `i` was declared before the loop, it still exists afterwards and holds the value that stopped the loop: 95, not 47. The `cout << endl;` after the loop ends the first line, so the last line is `5 passes, i = 95`.', 'hard', 'auto', '{"reserved":true,"compare":"trim_trailing","caseSensitive":true}', 1, 'published', 0, 1791590400000) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET topic_id = excluded.topic_id, lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, slug = excluded.slug, type = excluded.type, title = excluded.title, prompt_md = excluded.prompt_md, code = excluded.code, code_language = excluded.code_language, expected_behavior_md = excluded.expected_behavior_md, explanation_md = excluded.explanation_md, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, grading_mode = excluded.grading_mode, settings = excluded.settings, points = excluded.points, status = excluded.status, is_demo = excluded.is_demo, updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
